   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing a center\nfor technical assistance relating to age-friendly health systems; and in\nrelation to hospital performance data",
    "basePrintNo": "S5742",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5742-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§206 & 2995-b, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5742\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing a\ncenter for technical assistance relating to age-friendly health systems;\nand in relation to hospital performance data\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide incentives for the growth of age friendly health systems.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 shall be known as the \"age friendly health system enhancement\nact of 2024\"\n\nSection 2 adds a new section 2831 of the public health to provide grants\nto level two geriatric emergency departments.\n\nSection 3 adds a new paragraph (w) of subdivision 1 of section 206 of\nthe public health law to establish a center for technical assistance in\nrelation age friendly health systems in conjunction with the State\noffice for aging.\n\nSection 4. changes the title of section 2999-b of the public health law\nfrom hospital \"report cards\" to \"hospital performance data\" and adds a\nnew subdivision on special designations including age friendly status\n\nSection 5 is the immediate effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn the 2018 State of the State address, the Governor set a goal of\nmaking fifty percent of the all health systems age friendly within the\nnext five years. This goal has not achieved due in large part to the\nglobal pandemic. Progress has been, however, the state needs to provide\nincentives and focus to help spread the age friendly health system move-\nment. It provides for grants to hospitals that have geriatric emergency\ndepartments that achieve level two status and are on their way to level\nthree.\n\nThe legislation also establishes a center for technical assistance at\nthe Department of Health. This center must work together with the State\nOffice for Aging. The center could be staffed in the Department or\ncontracted out to qualified partners.\n\nThe bill also adds to special designations for hospitals by the Depart-\nment of Health, Hospitals that achieve age friendly status will be\nrecognized by the Department and noted on the official Department Legis-\nlative Information By providing these incentives, the state will hope-\nfully meet the goal set out in 2018.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA8474C of 2023 and 2024, referred to ways and means/Same as 58651Am\nreferred to health\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
